.TH "FAPOLICYD-RPM-PLUGIN" "8" "September 2026" "Red Hat" "System Administration Utilities"
.SH NAME
fapolicyd-rpm-plugin \- report RPM transaction changes to fapolicyd
.SH DESCRIPTION
The fapolicyd RPM transaction plugin sends metadata for files installed by
RPM to the fapolicyd daemon. It also requests trust database reloads and
object cache flushes at transaction and scriptlet boundaries.
.PP
The plugin is enabled by the
.B %__transaction_fapolicyd_rpm
RPM macro and is loaded from
.IR fapolicyd_rpm.so .
.SH COMMUNICATION
The plugin first connects to
.IR /run/fapolicyd/fapolicyd-update.fifo .
The daemon creates this endpoint with mode 0660.
.PP
During migration from the RPM-owned plugin, a previously started daemon may
still be listening on
.IR /run/fapolicyd/fapolicyd.fifo .
If the new endpoint does not exist, the plugin falls back to this legacy
endpoint. The fallback keeps package updates synchronized until the daemon is
restarted. A newly started daemon creates only the new endpoint, permanently
disabling the retired plugin.
.SH MIGRATION
Distributors should package this plugin with the daemon and replace the
RPM-owned
.B rpm-plugin-fapolicyd
package through normal package dependency metadata. The transition must not
restart an old daemon before the active RPM transaction plugin sends its final
records.
.PP
The complete cross-distribution procedure is documented in
.IR rpm-plugin-migration.md
in the fapolicyd source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fapolicyd (8),
.BR rpm-plugins (8)
